.\" man page create by R# package system.
.TH BIOSEQ.FASTA 4 2000-1月 "read_assembly" "read_assembly"
.SH NAME
read_assembly \- read genome assembly fasta sequence file
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIread_assembly(\fBfile\fR as any, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
read genome assembly fasta sequence file
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBfile\fB \fR\- 
 the file path of the genome assembly fasta sequence file, or a file stream 
 object of the target sequence file.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a named list of the @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.SequenceModel.NucleotideModels.ChunkedNtFasta\fR chunk sequence object, 
 the name of the list element is the fasta title of the corresponding 
 chromosome or contigs sequence.
 
 this function returns a R# error message object if the given file can not 
 be opened for read.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
unlike the \fBread.fasta\fR api, this function reads the whole genome 
 sequence in a chunked manner: the sequence data of each chromosome is 
 stored as a @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.SequenceModel.NucleotideModels.ChunkedNtFasta\fR object, so that we can slice a 
 sequence region from a huge chromosome sequence in a memory efficient 
 manner via the \fBslicer\fR api.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
bioseq.fasta
.SH FILES
.PP
seqtoolkit.dll
.PP
